<section class="wrap ff-standard-page"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Part selection guide</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">FIT & MEASURE</p><h1>Choosing replacement parts.</h1><p>Compare the part on your instrument with the product's measured drawings and specifications before ordering.</p><div class="ff-guide-list"><article><h2>01 / Compare the shape</h2><p>Check the full outline and housing footprint. Similar looking parts can have different mounting positions or clearances.</p></article><article><h2>02 / Check the dimensions</h2><p>Measure from the same points on both parts, using the same units. Distinguish string spacing from mounting hole spacing.</p></article><article><h2>03 / Confirm mounting</h2><p>Compare screw holes, pins, posts, thread pitch and cavity depth. For electronics, check the wiring and electrical values too.</p></article></div><div class="rte"><h2>By component</h2><h3>Tuning machines</h3><p>Check the headstock hole, bushing diameter, post height, rear screw or pin positions, and tuner orientation.</p><h3>Bridges and tailpieces</h3><p>Compare mounting hole centres, outside string spacing, bridge height, footprint and available cavity depth.</p><h3>Pickups and electronics</h3><p>Compare the pickup footprint, mounting ears, pole spacing, shaft dimensions, terminals, resistance and wiring.</p><h3>Pickguards and small hardware</h3><p>Compare the whole outline, each screw position, cutouts, bore size, shaft shape, thread pitch and included pieces.</p><p>Use the exact product variant's specifications for a purchase decision.</p></div></section>
